WEBVTT

00:07.424 --> 00:09.634
[gunfire and explosions]

00:13.096 --> 00:14.264
[chiming]

00:19.436 --> 00:20.478
[character 1] Drop that!

00:20.562 --> 00:22.397
- [commander] Go, go, go.
- Go, go, go!

00:25.025 --> 00:25.984
[character 2 groans]

00:26.067 --> 00:27.485
[commander] Code five!

00:29.362 --> 00:31.865
Son, you'll be late for the interview.

00:34.200 --> 00:35.827
[sighs heavily]

00:35.910 --> 00:38.246
Is killing people in a game
really fun for you?

00:38.329 --> 00:39.664
[Arisu grunts]

00:41.249 --> 00:42.417
Shit!

00:44.461 --> 00:45.587
Go, go, go, go!

00:53.803 --> 00:55.472
[heavy gunfire]

00:55.555 --> 00:57.932
[indistinct shouting]

00:58.016 --> 00:59.059
[man screams]

00:59.142 --> 01:01.352
- [gunfire continues]
- [panting]

01:01.436 --> 01:03.354
- [woman screaming]
- [glass smashing]

01:03.438 --> 01:05.023
Come on! Up the stairs! We can make it!

01:05.106 --> 01:06.441
[intense gunfire]

01:06.524 --> 01:07.567
Come on, run!

01:12.530 --> 01:14.115
[explosions and screaming]

01:14.199 --> 01:15.492
[man] Come on! Over--

01:17.160 --> 01:19.162
[explosions and gunfire continue]

01:21.623 --> 01:25.043
13 MINUTES AGO

01:29.130 --> 01:31.132
[wind gusting, paper fluttering]

01:39.015 --> 01:41.101
None of the games have started yet.

01:42.852 --> 01:44.479
Maybe we still have time.

01:45.105 --> 01:48.024
Or they forgot
to push the big red start button.

01:48.608 --> 01:51.277
They didn't even tell us
about the rules for this one.

01:52.153 --> 01:53.571
[sighs]

01:54.239 --> 01:56.241
[paper rustling]

01:58.493 --> 02:00.370
[wind gusting]

02:02.872 --> 02:04.874
[low rumbling]

02:06.000 --> 02:07.127
What is it?

02:07.210 --> 02:09.212
- [rumbling intensifying]
- [gasps]

02:10.713 --> 02:11.965
I hear something.

02:12.924 --> 02:14.926
[tense music]

02:28.314 --> 02:30.316
[deep rumbling]

02:37.866 --> 02:40.160
They're alive. Beach people.

02:47.792 --> 02:49.794
[engines throbbing]

02:56.342 --> 02:57.802
[rumbling fades]

03:09.647 --> 03:10.732
[Arisu] What is this?

03:11.983 --> 03:13.151
What are you doing here?

03:13.234 --> 03:14.611
We saw the blimps show up.

03:15.153 --> 03:17.614
There are rumors
that the next stage is starting.

03:18.364 --> 03:19.365
[Arisu] Right…

03:20.408 --> 03:21.326
Here's the thing--

03:21.409 --> 03:23.161
- [loud explosion]
- [Usagi yelps]

03:23.244 --> 03:24.454
Huh?

03:27.415 --> 03:28.625
Oh God!

03:28.708 --> 03:29.709
- [Yoshi screams]
- A rifle.

03:29.792 --> 03:31.252
- [man] What's happening?
- Get moving.

03:31.336 --> 03:32.712
[Taka] Run to the car!

03:32.795 --> 03:34.797
That thing's an anti-tank rifle.

03:35.632 --> 03:36.966
[screaming]

03:37.050 --> 03:41.012
- So I'd forget about hiding behind a car.
- What the hell?

03:41.095 --> 03:42.597
[Usagi] Where's it coming from?

03:43.806 --> 03:45.016
[Arisu] Run! Run!

03:45.558 --> 03:47.227
[rifle fire continues]

03:49.145 --> 03:51.481
- Does this mean the game's started?
- [Chishiya] I don't know.

03:51.564 --> 03:52.982
Did they give us any rules?

03:53.066 --> 03:55.568
[Arisu] Without rules,
this is just a massacre!

03:55.652 --> 03:57.654
[rifle fire continues]

03:58.279 --> 04:00.657
That rifle can kill from a kilometer away.

04:00.740 --> 04:02.492
- [machine-gun fire]
- [crowd screaming]

04:02.575 --> 04:05.328
Damn it, I recognize that sound.

04:05.411 --> 04:07.205
Now we've got an assault rifle.

04:07.288 --> 04:09.165
We have no idea how many there are.

04:09.249 --> 04:11.334
[Kuina] Other players are starting
to group together.

04:11.417 --> 04:13.586
- Could be more than one shooter.
- [man] Getting closer!

04:13.670 --> 04:16.297
[Kuina] I had no idea
so many players were still alive.

04:16.381 --> 04:17.548
[man] Run!

04:17.632 --> 04:19.467
- [Kuina gasps]
- They're almost here.

04:20.551 --> 04:21.844
We have to go!

04:21.928 --> 04:23.471
- Come on!
- [girl] Help me!

04:28.851 --> 04:29.811
[Arisu] Let's go!

04:31.562 --> 04:32.647
[Usagi] Arisu!

04:33.439 --> 04:34.899
- [groans]
- This is bad!

04:35.733 --> 04:37.318
[Chishiya] We need to split up!

04:55.461 --> 04:57.755
[commander] Kill, kill, kill, kill!
Go, go, go!

04:58.715 --> 05:00.633
[man] Go! Come on!

05:04.137 --> 05:05.430
[screaming]

05:26.743 --> 05:28.453
Arisu! Over here!

05:30.371 --> 05:31.998
[tense, pounding music]

05:48.848 --> 05:50.350
[gunfire continues]

05:57.774 --> 05:58.775
Aah!

05:59.275 --> 06:00.693
[groans]

06:01.402 --> 06:03.946
[Hajime] Hey.
You skip your interview again?

06:04.697 --> 06:07.116
If only reality could be reset. [scoffs]

06:10.495 --> 06:11.954
[panting and groaning]

06:13.706 --> 06:15.416
- [Usagi] Arisu!
- [burst of gunfire]

06:18.252 --> 06:20.254
[gunfire stops]

06:27.345 --> 06:28.971
[burst of gunfire]

06:29.972 --> 06:31.974
[gunfire stops]

06:39.440 --> 06:42.193
Are you trying to get killed out there?
[yelps]

06:43.736 --> 06:45.613
Where are they shooting from, anyway?

06:45.696 --> 06:47.365
[rumbling]

06:51.661 --> 06:54.872
Huh. He must be the King of Spades.

06:55.706 --> 06:57.708
[intense rumbling]

07:34.162 --> 07:36.164
[theme music]

08:36.182 --> 08:38.184
[rumbling continues]

08:43.648 --> 08:45.942
[Chishiya] Take this. A good luck charm.

08:46.984 --> 08:49.820
An explosive? You made this?

08:49.904 --> 08:51.489
Just use it if you have to.

08:53.324 --> 08:55.493
[gasps] Arisu! Now's our chance!

08:58.079 --> 08:59.163
[Arisu] Let's go!

09:03.000 --> 09:04.710
- Arisu?
- He's still alive!

09:06.712 --> 09:08.047
Hey! You okay?

09:08.631 --> 09:10.383
[pulses of energy]

09:11.259 --> 09:12.843
[silence]

09:14.220 --> 09:16.222
[tense music]

09:19.141 --> 09:20.810
The King of Spades is here.

09:21.477 --> 09:22.979
[low humming]

09:24.480 --> 09:25.940
[gasps] Come on!

09:26.607 --> 09:28.609
[Arisu] Hang in there! Get up!

09:29.860 --> 09:31.779
[gunfire resumes]

09:35.449 --> 09:36.784
[gunfire stops]

09:42.039 --> 09:43.207
You all right, huh?

09:44.834 --> 09:46.168
[running footsteps]

09:49.547 --> 09:51.507
[Kuina] Hey! You two okay? You hurt?

09:53.259 --> 09:54.468
[burst of gunfire]

09:54.552 --> 09:56.220
[man] Go! Go! Run!

09:59.807 --> 10:01.225
[Arisu] The King of Spades is

10:02.602 --> 10:04.061
just one guy.

10:07.148 --> 10:08.232
We're pinned down here!

10:08.316 --> 10:10.109
If we step out, he'll get us!

10:10.192 --> 10:11.902
- [horn honks]
- [vehicle drives up]

10:11.986 --> 10:12.862
Huh?

10:12.945 --> 10:14.280
[horn blares]

10:16.532 --> 10:17.950
[tires squeal]

10:20.369 --> 10:21.370
Get in!

10:21.454 --> 10:22.371
Tatta!

10:22.455 --> 10:24.081
- Don't just stand there!
- Ann!

10:29.545 --> 10:30.838
[whimpering]

10:30.921 --> 10:31.756
Run, Chishiya!

10:34.425 --> 10:35.468
That's bad. Get going!

10:35.551 --> 10:36.594
- Drive!
- Okay!

10:37.887 --> 10:39.138
Chishiya!

10:55.696 --> 10:57.239
Okay! We're safe for now.

10:57.323 --> 10:59.116
[sighs] You think Chishiya's okay?

10:59.200 --> 11:00.660
He can take care of himself.

11:00.743 --> 11:04.997
What kind of game is this, guys?
No rules. I mean, we didn't even register.

11:05.081 --> 11:07.958
- We just take the bad guys down, right?
- And how many are there?

11:08.042 --> 11:09.377
There's just the one.

11:10.753 --> 11:12.421
There's only one King of Spades.

11:12.922 --> 11:15.257
He's like the boss
of the physical challenges.

11:16.050 --> 11:18.928
During the attack,
the blimp was flying around.

11:19.553 --> 11:22.181
Maybe the battlefield
spans the whole city this time.

11:22.264 --> 11:24.558
How are we supposed to fight them
without a weapon?

11:24.642 --> 11:27.436
This next stage,
they really leveled up, huh?

11:28.646 --> 11:30.272
The next stage.

11:31.190 --> 11:35.444
Let's have some fun! All of us together!

11:35.528 --> 11:37.863
I mean, who is Mira? Is she human?

11:38.406 --> 11:39.615
I don't know.

11:39.699 --> 11:43.077
All I can say
is she might be one of the game masters.

11:43.160 --> 11:45.496
Mira? Game master?

11:45.579 --> 11:47.998
If we're right about the King of Spades,

11:48.499 --> 11:51.460
it's possible each suit has its own
game master at the top.

11:52.128 --> 11:55.506
We defeat all four,
we complete the next stage.

11:56.507 --> 11:57.466
We beat the bosses.

11:57.550 --> 11:58.718
Then what?

11:58.801 --> 12:00.010
We get to go home?

12:02.680 --> 12:03.931
I'm not sure yet.

12:04.473 --> 12:06.684
But that's our best chance to survive.

12:13.524 --> 12:16.026
Where are you even taking us, man?

12:16.110 --> 12:18.904
What? I'm following that car in front.

12:18.988 --> 12:22.366
- What? Is that a good idea? Who are they?
- Where should we go, then?

12:22.450 --> 12:25.703
Let's just be cool.
We escaped from the game and we're fine.

12:25.786 --> 12:27.747
That was not a game, Yui!

12:27.830 --> 12:31.250
What? We need a plan so we can win.

12:31.333 --> 12:32.418
We can't run away.

12:32.501 --> 12:35.463
That's not a bad idea. We've still got
plenty of days on our visas.

12:35.546 --> 12:36.547
That's true.

12:36.630 --> 12:39.633
- We hide until one of the others wins.
- Ooh! Yeah.

12:39.717 --> 12:40.968
[screams]

12:41.051 --> 12:42.428
[all gasping]

12:42.511 --> 12:44.263
[both screaming]

12:45.473 --> 12:47.391
[screams]

12:55.316 --> 12:58.194
Just because
we get through all the face cards safely,

12:58.277 --> 13:00.362
that doesn't mean we get to go back home.

13:01.030 --> 13:03.866
You don't believe
Hatter's bullshit now, do you?

13:03.949 --> 13:07.953
Yeah, but the next stage did start after
we got 40 different cards, like he said.

13:09.205 --> 13:12.124
[Arisu] None of us knew
what was going on when we got here.

13:12.208 --> 13:16.545
We figured out that winning games extended
our visas by the number of days on a card.

13:16.629 --> 13:19.215
If our visas run out,
we're killed by a laser.

13:19.799 --> 13:21.050
According to Hatter,

13:21.675 --> 13:25.930
collecting a whole deck of cards
would allow us to return home.

13:27.014 --> 13:29.058
The rules at least make sense.

13:29.683 --> 13:31.852
You just want it to be true.

13:31.936 --> 13:34.563
No, it's more than that.
There's a pattern.

13:35.314 --> 13:38.651
It seemed crazy,
but there were always rules.

13:48.953 --> 13:50.830
Hey, there's some Beach guys there.

13:52.790 --> 13:53.624
[all scream]

13:54.458 --> 13:55.584
Tatta! Go!

13:55.668 --> 13:56.919
Aah! Hold on!

13:57.002 --> 13:58.379
[Arisu] Tatta!

14:16.939 --> 14:19.108
- [screams]
- Hey! Tatta! Drive better!

14:19.191 --> 14:20.734
I can't!

14:25.406 --> 14:26.323
Let me drive now.

14:26.407 --> 14:28.033
- Eh?
- Now! Move!

14:28.117 --> 14:29.785
- Hey, careful. Shit!
- [Ann] Move!

14:31.704 --> 14:33.372
[both panting]

14:33.455 --> 14:34.456
Hang on.

14:49.430 --> 14:51.432
[tense, dramatic music]

14:54.018 --> 14:56.020
[tires screeching]

15:01.817 --> 15:03.068
[Usagi screams]

16:06.006 --> 16:07.007
He's not there!

16:07.716 --> 16:09.134
Hey. Nice one!

16:12.763 --> 16:14.056
[gasps] He's still there!

16:14.682 --> 16:15.599
[stamps on pedal]

16:33.784 --> 16:35.202
[Usagi screaming]

16:39.123 --> 16:40.833
Hey, Ann! Where are you taking us?

16:57.516 --> 16:58.392
[woman] Oh, shit!

17:10.195 --> 17:12.531
[Tatta yelling]

17:32.926 --> 17:34.470
[man] Hey, you guys okay?

17:35.679 --> 17:37.681
Holy shit! Did you see that?

17:40.225 --> 17:41.060
Anyone get hurt?

17:41.143 --> 17:42.811
[Tatta] Yeah, I twisted my neck.

17:43.312 --> 17:44.772
[Kuina] I broke a nail.

17:44.855 --> 17:46.190
- Oh shit--
- [gunfire]

17:56.575 --> 17:58.118
- [groans]
- [girl shrieks]

18:01.663 --> 18:03.248
- [man] Run!
- [gunfire continues]

18:08.420 --> 18:09.755
- [woman] They're--
- [gunfire]

18:13.550 --> 18:15.803
[whimpering] I can't do this!

18:15.886 --> 18:18.764
- I can't!
- If you stay here, you'll die. Come on.

18:18.847 --> 18:21.850
Even if I keep running,
there's always gonna be more!

18:21.934 --> 18:23.310
I can't do it!

18:29.149 --> 18:30.234
[Ann gasps]

18:31.777 --> 18:33.612
[burst of gunfire]

18:35.781 --> 18:38.408
[tense music]

18:41.495 --> 18:43.497
[gunfire continues]

18:47.334 --> 18:48.502
[screaming]

18:50.796 --> 18:52.506
[gunfire fades]

19:04.101 --> 19:07.521
[Arisu] I don't hear any more gunfire.
We should be safe for a while.

19:09.481 --> 19:11.525
- We can hide here.
- [Arisu] Good.

19:11.608 --> 19:13.235
[Kuina] I hope Chishiya's okay.

19:13.318 --> 19:14.653
And Ann, too.

19:14.736 --> 19:18.574
Oh, I'm sure they're fine.
I mean, they're, like, super smart.

19:18.657 --> 19:19.616
You're right.

19:20.117 --> 19:21.326
If we're staying here,

19:21.827 --> 19:24.246
we'll have to go out
and scavenge some supplies.

19:24.329 --> 19:25.330
Water, food.

19:25.914 --> 19:26.832
[Arisu] Mm-hmm.

19:27.708 --> 19:30.460
Oh man, this sucks. Do we have to, though?

19:31.336 --> 19:34.339
The longer we wait,
the more likely it is that he'll show up.

19:35.132 --> 19:36.884
Let's go find some food.

19:37.968 --> 19:40.429
And I'll… I'll go find us a ride.

19:41.221 --> 19:42.556
Coming with me?

19:42.639 --> 19:43.682
What?

19:43.765 --> 19:45.893
Well, there's a place near here.

19:45.976 --> 19:47.769
Okay, fine.

19:51.398 --> 19:54.526
We won't be long.
You'd better bring back something good.

19:54.610 --> 19:56.028
- We will.
- Here.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.237
Oh, cool.

19:57.321 --> 19:59.740
- [sighs] Okay, let's go.
- Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

19:59.823 --> 20:02.326
Let me guess. You've never had
a hot girl on your arm before?

20:02.409 --> 20:04.703
- Come on.
- Sure I have. Shut up!

20:12.586 --> 20:15.130
[Tatta] Okay, this is the spot.
Nice, right?

20:15.214 --> 20:18.175
[Kuina] Yeah, nice.
Lots of old cars. Cool.

20:18.258 --> 20:20.552
[Tatta] Hey!
They're not old, they're classic.

20:20.636 --> 20:21.887
[Kuina] Who cares?

20:27.643 --> 20:29.853
[Tatta] Wait. Are you kidding me?

20:30.520 --> 20:32.898
Holy shit!

20:32.981 --> 20:35.108
Just look at her curves! Oh!

20:35.192 --> 20:37.778
Dude, don't be weird. It's just a car.

20:37.861 --> 20:40.364
Whoa! Have you ever seen
something this hot?

20:40.447 --> 20:42.324
That's so gross.

20:45.577 --> 20:46.620
[sighs]

20:46.703 --> 20:48.789
You know, I realized the other day,

20:48.872 --> 20:51.875
rich people are probably the ones
who are suffering the most now.

20:52.626 --> 20:56.129
Everything they built, that mattered
to them, it's all worthless now.

20:57.214 --> 20:58.423
You're right. [sighs]

20:59.132 --> 21:00.550
I guess I'm lucky, then.

21:01.051 --> 21:03.220
Don't have to worry about rent anymore.

21:03.762 --> 21:07.224
Yeah, me too. No more credit card
interest payments either.

21:08.267 --> 21:09.268
[chuckles]

21:13.021 --> 21:13.855
You know what?

21:17.776 --> 21:20.862
Even with all the bills and payments,
I still want to go home.

21:21.488 --> 21:22.739
[sighs]

21:25.158 --> 21:26.159
Yeah, me too.

21:30.122 --> 21:31.832
[wind whistling]

21:54.271 --> 21:57.190
YAKISOBA KORE! BAN
SHORTCAKE FLAVOR

21:57.941 --> 21:59.109
[chuckles]

22:00.235 --> 22:02.404
[Chota] Cake-flavored yakisoba?

22:03.155 --> 22:05.574
Oh, it's just like the one
in the commercial!

22:05.657 --> 22:07.909
- Oh, yeah!
- [both laugh]

22:07.993 --> 22:11.121
What are you doing there?
You know how gross those flavors turn out?

22:11.997 --> 22:14.416
Oh, I beg to differ! [laughs]

22:14.499 --> 22:15.876
- Mm.
- [Chota chuckles]

22:15.959 --> 22:17.127
You're such a virgin.

22:17.711 --> 22:19.254
Yo, that is so uncalled-for.

22:20.339 --> 22:22.215
- Hey, you better eat it all.
- Oh, for sure.

22:22.299 --> 22:23.842
- All of it.
- I won't have any problem.

22:23.925 --> 22:25.302
- You sure?
- None. Arisu will help.

22:25.385 --> 22:26.261
Come on, seriously?

22:26.345 --> 22:28.347
[quiet, poignant music]

22:28.430 --> 22:31.058
[wind whistling]

22:37.439 --> 22:39.232
Come on, seriously? [chuckles]

23:00.003 --> 23:01.463
[laughs] Cash or credit?

23:02.964 --> 23:04.049
[laughs]

23:05.884 --> 23:08.387
[Arisu] That's good.
I haven't heard that in a long time.

23:08.470 --> 23:10.472
[chuckles] Here.

23:15.602 --> 23:16.770
Is this stuff good?

23:17.521 --> 23:19.106
Mm-hmm. I think so.

23:20.065 --> 23:21.149
[Usagi] Hmm.

23:23.777 --> 23:25.320
How many chopsticks would you like?

23:26.279 --> 23:28.240
I'll take four sets, please.

23:28.323 --> 23:29.491
[Usagi] Of course, sir.

23:32.828 --> 23:35.080
Thank you very much,
and I hope you have a wonderful day.

23:35.831 --> 23:38.708
What was-- Your voice went up,
like, a whole octave there.

23:39.292 --> 23:42.087
But it makes you wanna buy more, right?
[laughs]

23:43.130 --> 23:45.799
Yeah, I bet a ton of guys
would have come in for you.

23:45.882 --> 23:46.967
With that smile.

23:47.551 --> 23:49.302
- Huh?
- Huh?

23:52.597 --> 23:53.974
Hey, are you blushing?

23:54.474 --> 23:56.852
No. I'm used to it.

23:57.602 --> 23:58.520
Really?

23:59.563 --> 24:01.022
[both laugh]

24:03.817 --> 24:04.818
[Usagi sighs]

24:06.695 --> 24:09.406
I always wanted to work
at a convenience store.

24:09.489 --> 24:11.032
- Seriously?
- Mm-hmm.

24:11.867 --> 24:13.952
The barcodes. I like scanning.

24:14.035 --> 24:15.328
[both chuckle]

24:15.412 --> 24:17.372
You know the ones
who could scan real well?

24:17.456 --> 24:19.207
- I really admired them.
- Ah, yeah.

24:19.291 --> 24:20.459
And here you are, sir.

24:22.794 --> 24:25.589
I can't wait
to get back to our world. [sighs]

24:27.966 --> 24:30.385
Eating yakisoba, AC on full blast,

24:30.469 --> 24:32.471
sitting with your best friends,

24:33.305 --> 24:35.599
reading all the new manga
when they come out.

24:37.392 --> 24:38.602
[sighs]

24:41.980 --> 24:43.982
[slurping]

24:47.444 --> 24:49.613
- Stop doin' that, man.
- [chuckles]

24:49.696 --> 24:51.740
- Creepy smiling makes me wanna hurl.
- Mmm, mmm.

24:52.407 --> 24:53.575
Yeah, stop.

24:54.576 --> 24:56.912
- Look at this right here. See?
- Huh? Hm.

24:56.995 --> 25:00.165
The look on her face.
Her breasts, are you seeing them?

25:00.248 --> 25:01.458
She's a total ten, bro!

25:01.541 --> 25:05.378
[Karube] Manga magazines should be
about the manga, not the models.

25:05.462 --> 25:08.173
- [Chota] That's not true.
- What are you talking about? Let me check.

25:08.256 --> 25:09.841
[snorts and laughs]

25:09.925 --> 25:12.135
- You see? She's hot.
- [mimics choking] You hearing this?

25:12.219 --> 25:13.428
- Karube.
- What was that?

25:13.512 --> 25:14.513
- Check it out.
- Good stuff.

25:14.596 --> 25:15.764
- What?
- [Arisu] Look, here.

25:15.847 --> 25:16.723
- You see?
- Arisu.

25:17.474 --> 25:20.393
You keep saying stupid shit like this,
you'll catch the virgin.

25:20.477 --> 25:22.020
- Wait, what?
- Oh, no, not the virgin!

25:22.103 --> 25:23.980
- Virgin isn't a disease!
- Oh, no!

25:24.064 --> 25:25.607
- Damn, you've got it now!
- I guess I did.

25:25.690 --> 25:27.150
- Wait! I'm already a virgin!
- Oh shit!

25:27.234 --> 25:29.194
- Oh, now we're teaming up!
- I'm gonna get you…

25:32.906 --> 25:34.449
[chuckles]

25:34.533 --> 25:36.785
Man, those were some good times.

25:43.333 --> 25:44.459
Usagi…

25:48.004 --> 25:50.048
We're gonna make it back to our world.

25:50.549 --> 25:52.509
[faint thumping]

25:54.886 --> 25:56.721
[clattering]

25:59.015 --> 26:00.141
What's wrong?

26:01.977 --> 26:04.020
- [rustling]
- [breathing shakily]

26:07.274 --> 26:08.358
[rustling]

26:12.862 --> 26:16.533
KENICHIRO SHIBASAKI ATTEMPTS SUICIDE
OVER FALSE ARTICLE

26:18.326 --> 26:19.536
- [gasps]
- [Usagi] Dad…

26:23.832 --> 26:25.458
- [reporters clamoring]
- Mr. Usagi?

26:25.542 --> 26:27.043
Do you have any comment?

26:27.127 --> 26:28.086
[door slams]

26:29.671 --> 26:33.341
[newsreader 1] A mountain climber has
gone missing while climbing Mt. Tanigawa

26:33.425 --> 26:35.760
on the border between Gunma and Niigata…

26:35.844 --> 26:36.886
AN OXYGEN TANK WAS USED

26:36.970 --> 26:38.680
"SOLO NO-OXYGEN ASCENT"
WAS IT ALL A HOAX!?

26:38.763 --> 26:40.890
[newsreader 1] …the man is famed climber
Shigenori Usagi

26:40.974 --> 26:44.019
whose accomplishments include
climbing Mt. Everest and as a guide…

26:44.102 --> 26:46.271
SHIGENORI USAGI:
SUICIDE AFTER SUSPICIONS OF DECEIT?

26:46.354 --> 26:47.522
SUICIDE?

26:47.606 --> 26:49.941
[newsreader 2] …continue to conduct
ground and air searches,

26:50.025 --> 26:51.943
but so far have not turned up anything…

26:52.027 --> 26:54.279
[newsreader 1] There are no leads
in the search for Usagi,

26:54.362 --> 26:56.698
who went missing climbing Mt. Tanigawa.

26:56.781 --> 26:58.116
- [clamor of voices]
- [Arisu] Usagi?

26:59.242 --> 27:01.244
[paper rustling]

27:02.787 --> 27:04.122
Uh, what is it?

27:08.960 --> 27:10.545
[sighs] Arisu…

27:13.256 --> 27:15.884
Did you really love your life so much?

27:17.093 --> 27:18.053
Huh?

27:19.929 --> 27:21.014
[sighs]

27:22.974 --> 27:24.643
I lost my dad…

27:28.688 --> 27:30.565
right before all this.

27:32.692 --> 27:33.777
[sighs]

27:36.112 --> 27:37.489
They called him a liar.

27:41.242 --> 27:43.787
They harassed him too,
never left him alone.

27:45.580 --> 27:46.915
He went for a climb.

27:51.920 --> 27:53.380
And he never came back.

27:55.006 --> 27:56.508
That was the last I heard.

28:00.804 --> 28:02.806
- [sighs]
- [paper rustling]

28:03.598 --> 28:05.684
But he'd been out so many times.

28:10.146 --> 28:12.524
And it wasn't a tough mountain at all.

28:14.484 --> 28:17.153
It's impossible,
that's what I told myself.

28:19.406 --> 28:20.365
But now…

28:21.950 --> 28:24.202
After living here, I understand.

28:26.663 --> 28:27.747
[gasps]

28:28.540 --> 28:29.708
He hated this world.

28:33.461 --> 28:34.671
And he wanted…

28:38.007 --> 28:40.468
He hoped he could find a different one.

28:44.431 --> 28:46.516
I never thought about that before.

28:46.599 --> 28:47.934
[breathing shakily]

28:52.021 --> 28:53.231
And that's…

28:55.275 --> 28:56.818
That's how I feel, too.

28:59.654 --> 29:01.865
I didn't realize
how much I hated our world.

29:05.285 --> 29:07.537
If we went back, I'd still hate it there.

29:09.164 --> 29:10.623
[inhales shakily]

29:11.624 --> 29:12.709
[sighs]

29:15.920 --> 29:17.505
I'm sorry. I…

29:19.674 --> 29:21.968
Getting back is something
everyone else wants.

29:31.936 --> 29:32.896
Usagi.

29:35.106 --> 29:36.691
I know how you feel.

29:38.485 --> 29:39.360
I do.

29:43.281 --> 29:45.033
I hated so much of my life.

29:45.784 --> 29:47.160
The world was shit.

29:48.745 --> 29:50.121
But now, I don't know.

29:51.414 --> 29:52.582
Since coming here,

29:54.042 --> 29:55.710
I wanna try again.

29:57.754 --> 29:59.589
I wanna be a better person.

30:06.304 --> 30:07.722
I'll protect you.

30:08.389 --> 30:09.808
I'll do whatever it takes.

30:11.935 --> 30:13.394
Let's go back together.

30:26.866 --> 30:28.076
I'm sorry.

30:30.954 --> 30:32.247
[sighs]

30:32.330 --> 30:34.040
Everyone says it, Arisu.

30:35.375 --> 30:37.293
That they know how I feel.

30:38.294 --> 30:41.130
That I should just forget the past
and be happy.

30:47.762 --> 30:50.348
[tearfully] But it's not so easy
to forget.

30:52.892 --> 30:54.018
Even you…

30:56.563 --> 30:58.982
I don't know
what you've been through either.

31:03.611 --> 31:06.865
If someone understands me or not,
it doesn't make a difference.

31:09.534 --> 31:10.535
It's just…

31:14.622 --> 31:17.417
if somebody gave me the chance
to go back there…

31:19.794 --> 31:21.212
to that world…

31:27.594 --> 31:29.512
I really don't think that I would.

31:31.097 --> 31:33.016
Staying here won't change that.

31:33.099 --> 31:34.434
- Usagi…
- [gasps]

31:35.685 --> 31:36.811
[Usagi breathing shakily]

31:42.066 --> 31:43.818
[quiet, somber music]

31:47.113 --> 31:48.865
[sighs] We should go.

31:50.742 --> 31:52.035
Everyone's waiting.

32:19.938 --> 32:22.023
[engine rumbling]

32:29.489 --> 32:32.909
[Tatta] Hey, hey! Arisu! Usagi! Get in!

32:33.785 --> 32:36.913
- [Kuina] We're exposed in this thing.
- [Tatta] It's the only one I could start.

32:36.996 --> 32:39.666
You are such a liar.
I watched you fall in love with it.

32:39.749 --> 32:41.417
It was so gross the way you felt it up.

32:41.501 --> 32:43.753
- Said it was sexy…
- [Tatta] I said I liked its curves.

32:43.836 --> 32:45.463
- [Kuina] Dude, that's so gross.
- [chuckles]

32:45.546 --> 32:48.049
[Tatta] What do you mean, gross?
I like the car.

32:51.094 --> 32:52.136
Get in.

32:57.892 --> 32:59.894
- [opens car door]
- [Tatta] Arisu?

33:00.812 --> 33:01.854
Uh, yeah.

33:08.069 --> 33:10.196
[revs engine]

33:25.878 --> 33:27.630
[low, intense rumbling]

33:40.643 --> 33:42.645
[dramatic music]

34:06.794 --> 34:09.088
[Arisu] The King of Spades
is getting closer.

34:10.214 --> 34:13.593
It's just like you said.
His arena is the whole city.

34:16.304 --> 34:19.932
That's not good.
We gotta stay ahead of him, keep running.

34:22.602 --> 34:25.271
[Arisu] There's another way
we can stay off his radar.

34:26.022 --> 34:26.898
What's that?

34:28.357 --> 34:30.443
There's other games we can join, right?

34:30.943 --> 34:31.819
Huh?

34:33.905 --> 34:36.032
Put yourself in their shoes for a sec.

34:36.699 --> 34:39.160
I wouldn't want my game interfered with.

34:39.911 --> 34:42.622
So they have some kind of agreement,
is that it?

34:43.873 --> 34:46.125
Don't interfere with each other,
be polite.

34:47.543 --> 34:51.380
Each game so far has had rules.
Very strict rules.

34:52.256 --> 34:54.217
If another game got mixed in,

34:55.051 --> 34:56.803
it would completely ruin it.

34:57.595 --> 34:58.930
[Tatta] But, like…

34:59.680 --> 35:02.016
What if I don't wanna play anymore?

35:02.100 --> 35:06.104
[Kuina] We were forced into
the King of Spades' game, like it or not.

35:06.854 --> 35:08.731
We can keep hiding, sure.

35:08.815 --> 35:11.150
But eventually, he'll find us and kill us,

35:11.234 --> 35:13.986
or our visas will run out,
and then, pyeow!

35:14.612 --> 35:16.405
[Arisu] If we keep playing, though,

35:16.906 --> 35:19.242
we'll be able to get more information.

35:19.325 --> 35:22.078
Find out from the game masters
what this place is.

35:22.620 --> 35:24.455
Or why we're here.

35:26.124 --> 35:27.625
We need more answers.

35:29.752 --> 35:31.587
Or everyone else died for nothing.

35:43.391 --> 35:44.767
Why don't we vote on it?

35:47.145 --> 35:48.980
I'm with Arisu on this.

35:51.566 --> 35:52.692
Oh shit.

35:54.235 --> 35:56.529
All right. Count me in.

35:56.612 --> 35:57.572
[sighs]

35:58.197 --> 35:59.115
Usagi?

36:03.119 --> 36:04.620
It's majority rules.

36:05.288 --> 36:06.581
You have your answer.

36:09.375 --> 36:12.044
So, which game first? What do you think?

36:16.841 --> 36:20.386
[Arisu] The furthest one we can see
is here, along the harbor.

36:21.387 --> 36:22.680
The King of Clubs.

36:23.431 --> 36:26.184
You're picking a King? You're joking?

36:26.267 --> 36:29.353
A King would probably
have more key information.

36:29.437 --> 36:31.856
[sighs] You've got guts, Arisu.

36:31.939 --> 36:35.610
And besides,
Club games are about teamwork.

36:36.652 --> 36:38.446
So we'll have a chance to win.

36:39.655 --> 36:42.491
- With this group, for sure!
- Ah! Yeah!

36:42.575 --> 36:44.076
I'm not counting you in that.

36:44.577 --> 36:46.120
- [Tatta] Hey!
- [Kuina] Kidding!

36:55.004 --> 36:57.006
[dramatic music]

38:01.279 --> 38:02.405
What's that?

38:16.043 --> 38:18.004
NO WEAPONS ALLOWED

38:18.713 --> 38:21.048
PARTICIPANTS: FIVE PLAYERS
PLEASE PUT ON BRACELETS AND WAIT

38:21.132 --> 38:22.174
[Arisu] Bracelets?

38:23.676 --> 38:25.803
[Kuina] It says we need five players.

38:26.304 --> 38:27.805
But there's only four.

38:30.349 --> 38:31.809
[man] Five, actually.

38:37.106 --> 38:38.232
Niragi?

38:38.816 --> 38:40.109
It's been a while.

38:43.404 --> 38:44.655
What?

38:45.323 --> 38:46.365
You're still alive?

38:49.035 --> 38:51.495
Team up with him? I don't think so.

38:52.163 --> 38:54.081
[Tatta] He'll sabotage us, for sure.

38:55.791 --> 38:57.918
I bet he's already got
a plan to screw us over.

38:58.002 --> 39:00.254
The bracelet's not comin' off now.

39:02.673 --> 39:04.925
All I wanna do is enjoy the game.

39:06.802 --> 39:08.763
If you're not interested in playin',

39:09.263 --> 39:11.599
you'd better get outta here, huh?

39:16.562 --> 39:17.688
[Kuina] Usagi?

39:18.814 --> 39:20.566
[Usagi] I don't care what he wants.

39:22.693 --> 39:24.695
[whirs]

39:27.990 --> 39:29.825
If we don't join the game,

39:30.534 --> 39:31.786
we'll be gunned down.

39:33.621 --> 39:34.914
And that's it.

39:36.957 --> 39:39.418
I'd rather fight here
than die like an animal.

39:44.924 --> 39:45.841
Me too.

39:50.137 --> 39:51.430
I wanna know why.

39:59.897 --> 40:01.440
[whirs]

40:07.446 --> 40:08.489
[sighs]

40:08.989 --> 40:10.574
You two are idiots.

40:11.784 --> 40:13.452
Don't say I didn't warn you.

40:16.288 --> 40:17.331
[sighs]

40:18.874 --> 40:20.251
Hey, don't slow us down.

40:21.335 --> 40:23.754
This game is about working together.

40:25.756 --> 40:28.509
And I'm pretty sure you're the slow one.

40:33.931 --> 40:35.641
[loud rumbling]

40:36.851 --> 40:39.145
[female announcer]
Registration is now closed.

40:39.228 --> 40:41.397
The game will now commence.

40:48.028 --> 40:50.030
[echoing crash]

41:01.667 --> 41:02.668
[chime]

41:03.919 --> 41:07.214
[chimes continue]

41:11.927 --> 41:13.929
[machinery rumbles loudly]

41:46.962 --> 41:48.589
[Tatta] What is this place?

41:53.969 --> 41:57.389
[announcer] The King of Club's team
is now entering the field.

41:57.473 --> 41:58.849
[rock music]

42:19.370 --> 42:20.496
[man] Welcome…

42:22.623 --> 42:24.375
to our game field.

42:26.460 --> 42:28.128
I am the King of Clubs,

42:29.338 --> 42:30.464
Kyuma.

42:40.683 --> 42:42.309
- Uh…
- Uh…

42:42.393 --> 42:43.394
[exhales]

42:43.477 --> 42:44.478
[gasps]

42:45.271 --> 42:48.107
Okay, let me introduce everyone.

42:48.190 --> 42:50.109
First we have Shitara.

42:54.196 --> 42:55.281
Uta.

42:56.740 --> 42:57.700
Maki.

42:58.993 --> 43:00.160
Goken.

43:03.581 --> 43:04.498
Pleasure.

43:08.335 --> 43:10.087
That's all the reaction I get?

43:10.754 --> 43:12.423
I think you're weirding them out.

43:12.506 --> 43:13.924
Put some damn pants on.

43:14.508 --> 43:16.260
[Kyuma] What? Not a chance!

43:16.844 --> 43:18.929
Nudism is an upstanding practice.

43:19.013 --> 43:21.682
A social movement
with hundreds of years of history!

43:22.933 --> 43:25.436
Clothing is a social construct.

43:25.519 --> 43:27.688
No biological necessity.

43:28.606 --> 43:31.066
Humans should be bare and raw.

43:31.150 --> 43:33.152
After all, it's only natural.

43:34.445 --> 43:36.363
What's the deal with this guy?

43:37.740 --> 43:39.950
So this is the King of Clubs?

43:40.034 --> 43:41.869
Out of his damn mind.

43:43.245 --> 43:47.333
Listen, we don't care about that.
Just tell us who you are.

43:50.377 --> 43:51.629
Who are we?

43:52.671 --> 43:54.548
We are the citizens of this country.

43:57.509 --> 43:58.677
Citizens?

43:59.178 --> 44:01.263
Sure. Citizens.

44:15.027 --> 44:17.154
[theme music]
